<title>JAPAN: June Daqing crude calculated at $17.40--traders.</title>
<headline>June Daqing crude calculated at $17.40--traders.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Daqing crude oil price for June-lifting to Japanese customers has been calculated at $17.40 per barrel, down 98 cents from May when it was $18.38, oil traders in Tokyo said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Japanese buyers have accepted a Chinese offer to allocate them six million to eight million tonnes per year for the 1996 to 2000 period.</p>
<p>China reviews its Daqing export volume every five years.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3706</p>
